            <ArticleTitle>Pain management in newborns: how far have we progressed in research and practice?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Compelling research supports the newborn infant's capacity for pain. Yet, pain is frequently underestimated and undertreated. This is a result of limited understanding of pain pathway development, immediate and long-term consequences, measurement tools and approaches, and safety and efficacy of pain-relieving interventions. This paper reviews recent research in relation to management of pain in the newborn, and presents implications for practice and future research.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
